{"id":"mahabharata-7-172","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":172,"title":"द्विसप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 172 · Ashvatthaman's Agneya weapon and Vyasa's explanation","summary":{"en":"Ashvatthaman hurls the Agneya weapon, and Arjuna answers with the Brahma weapon, and Vyasa appears to explain the matter. He tells Ashvatthaman that Arjuna and Krishna are Nara and Narayana, and describes Shiva's greatness, and Ashvatthaman is stilled.","kn":"ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಆಗ್ನೇಯಾಸ್ತ್ರ ಎಸೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಾಸ್ತ್ರದಿಂದ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವ್ಯಾಸರು ಪ್ರತ್ಯಕ್ಷರಾಗಿ ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನ-ಕೃಷ್ಣರು ನರ-ನಾರಾಯಣರೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಶಿವನ ಮಹಿಮೆಯನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸಿದಾಗ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಶಾಂತನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अश्वत्थामा आग्नेयास्त्र फेंकता है और अर्जुन ब्रह्मास्त्र से उत्तर देते हैं, तभी व्यास प्रकट होकर समझाते हैं। वे अश्वत्थामा को बताते हैं कि अर्जुन और कृष्ण नर और नारायण हैं और शिव की महिमा बताते हैं, और अश्वत्थामा शान्त होता है।","te":"అశ్వత్థామ ఆగ్నేయాస్త్రం విసురుతాడు; అర్జునుడు బ్రహ్మాస్త్రంతో బదులిస్తాడు; వ్యాసుడు ప్రత్యక్షమై వివరిస్తాడు. అర్జున కృష్ణులు నర నారాయణులని, శివుని మహిమను చెప్పగా అశ్వత్థామ శాంతిస్తాడు.","ta":"அஸ்வத்தாமன் ஆக்னேயாஸ்திரத்தை எய்ய, அர்ஜுனன் பிரம்மாஸ்திரத்தால் பதிலளிக்க, வியாசர் தோன்றி விளக்குகிறார். அர்ஜுனனும் கண்ணனும் நர நாராயணர் என்றும் சிவனின் பெருமையையும் கூறியதும் அஸ்வத்தாமன் அமைதியடைகிறான்.","ml":"അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് ആഗ്നേയാസ്ത്രം പ്രയോഗിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനൻ ബ്രഹ്മാസ്ത്രംകൊണ്ട് മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; കാര്യം വിശദീകരിക്കാൻ വ്യാസൻ പ്രത്യക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു. അർജുനനും കൃഷ്ണനും നര-നാരായണന്മാരാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം അശ്വത്ഥാമാവിനോട് പറയുന്നു, ശിവന്റെ മഹത്വം വിവരിക്കുന്നു; അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് ശാന്തനാകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.172; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"नारायणास्त्रमोक्षपर्व","titleEn":"Narayanastramoksha Parva (Release of the Narayana weapon)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तत्प्रभग्नं बलं दृष्ट्वा कुन्तीपुत्रो धनंजयः ।\nन्यवारयदमेयात्मा द्रोणपुत्रवधेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that army broken, Dhananjaya, son of Kunti, of immeasurable soul, held them back, wishing to kill Drona's son."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततस्ते सैनिका राजन्नैव तत्रावतस्थिरे ।\nसंस्थाप्यमाना यत्नेन गोविन्देनार्जुनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet, O king, those soldiers did not stay there, though Govinda and Arjuna tried hard to steady them."}},{"n":3,"text":"एक एव तु बीभत्सुः सोमकावयवैः सह ।\nमत्स्यैरन्यैश्च संधाय कौरवैः संन्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu alone, with some Somakas, and the Matsyas and others, made a pact with some Kauravas and turned back."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो द्रुतमतिक्रम्य सिंहलाङ्गूलकेतनम् ।\nसव्यसाची महेष्वासमश्वत्थामानमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, swiftly passing by Ashvatthaman, the great archer with the lion's-tail banner, Savyasachi said to him:"}},{"n":5,"text":"या शक्तिर्यच्च ते वीर्यं यज्ज्ञानं यच्च पौरुषम् ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रेषु या प्रीतिः प्रद्वेषोऽस्मासु यश्च ते ।\nयच्च भूयोऽस्ति तेजस्तत्परमं मम दर्शय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said: Whatever strength, valour, knowledge and manliness you have, whatever love you bear for Dhritarashtra's sons and hatred for us, and whatever further power you have, show me that supreme."}},{"n":6,"text":"स एव द्रोणहन्ता ते दर्पं भेत्स्यति पार्षतः ।\nकालानलसमप्रख्यो द्विषतामन्तको युधि ।\nसमासादय पाञ्चाल्यं मां चापि सहकेशवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That same son of Prishata, slayer of Drona, will break your pride, he who is like the fire of Time and the destroyer of enemies in battle. Face the Panchala, and me too, together with Keshava."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"आचार्यपुत्रो मानार्हो बलवांश्चापि संजय ।\nप्रीतिर्धनंजये चास्य प्रियश्चापि स वासवेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, the teacher's son is worthy of honour and strong; he has affection for Dhananjaya, and is dear to Vasava's son."}},{"n":8,"text":"न भूतपूर्वं बीभत्सोर्वाक्यं परुषमीदृशम् ।\nअथ कस्मात्स कौन्तेयः सखायं रूक्षमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such harsh words from Bibhatsu were never heard before. Why then did that son of Kunti speak roughly to his friend?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"युवराजे हते चैव वृद्धक्षत्रे च पौरवे ।\nइष्वस्त्रविधिसंपन्ने मालवे च सुदर्शने ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the crown prince killed, and Vriddhakshatra, and the Paurava, and the Malava Sudarshana skilled in arrows and weapons,"}},{"n":10,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्ने सात्यकौ च भीमे चापि पराजिते ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य तैर्वाक्यैर्मर्मण्यपि च घट्टिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"and with Dhrishtadyumna, Satyaki and Bhima defeated, and his vitals struck even by Yudhishthira's words,"}},{"n":11,"text":"अन्तर्भेदे च संजाते दुःखं संस्मृत्य च प्रभो ।\nअभूतपूर्वो बीभत्सोर्दुःखान्मन्युरजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"and an inner rift having arisen, remembering his grief, lord, an anger never known before arose in Bibhatsu out of sorrow."}},{"n":12,"text":"तस्मादनर्हमश्लीलमप्रियं द्रौणिमुक्तवान् ।\nमान्यमाचार्यतनयं रूक्षं कापुरुषो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, like a base man, he spoke to Drona's son, the honoured son of his teacher, in an undeserving, unseemly, unkind and rough way."}},{"n":13,"text":"एवमुक्तः श्वसन्क्रोधान्महेष्वासतमो नृप ।\nपार्थेन परुषं वाक्यं सर्वमर्मघ्नया गिरा ।\nद्रौणिश्चुकोप पार्थाय कृष्णाय च विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to so, the great archer sighed in anger, O king; at Partha's harsh words which pierced every vital spot, Drona's son grew angry at Partha, and especially at Krishna."}},{"n":14,"text":"स तु यत्तो रथे स्थित्वा वार्युपस्पृश्य वीर्यवान् ।\nदेवैरपि सुदुर्धर्षमस्त्रमाग्नेयमाददे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing alert in his chariot and touching water, that mighty one took up the Agneya weapon, hard to withstand even for the gods."}},{"n":15,"text":"दृश्यादृश्यानरिगणानुद्दिश्याचार्यनन्दनः ।\nसोऽभिमन्त्र्य शरं दीप्तं विधूममिव पावकम् ।\nसर्वतः क्रोधमाविश्य चिक्षेप परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The teacher's son, aiming it at foes seen and unseen, charmed a blazing arrow like smokeless fire, entered a rage on every side, and the slayer of enemy heroes hurled it."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततस्तुमुलमाकाशे शरवर्षमजायत ।\nववुश्च शिशिरा वाताः सूर्यो नैव तताप च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a tumultuous shower of arrows arose in the sky; cool winds blew, and the sun gave no heat."}},{"n":17,"text":"चुक्रुशुर्दानवाश्चापि दिक्षु सर्वासु भैरवम् ।\nरुधिरं चापि वर्षन्तो विनेदुस्तोयदाम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The danavas too cried out fearfully in all directions, and clouds in the sky rumbled, raining blood."}},{"n":18,"text":"पक्षिणः पशवो गावो मुनयश्चापि सुव्रताः ।\nपरमं प्रयतात्मानो न शान्तिमुपलेभिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Birds, beasts, cows and sages of good vows, though of the most self-controlled mind, found no peace."}},{"n":19,"text":"भ्रान्तसर्वमहाभूतमावर्जितदिवाकरम् ।\nत्रैलोक्यमभिसंतप्तं ज्वराविष्टमिवातुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the great elements were disturbed, the sun was turned aside, and the three worlds were scorched, like a sick man seized with fever."}},{"n":20,"text":"शरतेजोऽभिसंतप्ता नागा भूमिशयास्तथा ।\nनिःश्वसन्तः समुत्पेतुस्तेजो घोरं मुमुक्षवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Snakes lying on the ground, scorched by the blaze of the arrows, sighed and leapt up, wishing to be freed from the fearful heat."}},{"n":21,"text":"जलजानि च सत्त्वानि दह्यमानानि भारत ।\nन शान्तिमुपजग्मुर्हि तप्यमानैर्जलाशयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Water-born creatures were burning, O Bharata, and found no peace, as the waters themselves were being heated."}},{"n":22,"text":"दिशः खं प्रदिशश्चैव भुवं च शरवृष्टयः ।\nउच्चावचा निपेतुर्वै गरुडानिलरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showers of arrows fell of every sort, on directions, sky, intermediate directions and earth, with the speed of Garuda and the wind."}},{"n":23,"text":"तैः शरैर्द्रोणपुत्रस्य वज्रवेगसमाहितैः ।\nप्रदग्धाः शत्रवः पेतुरग्निदग्धा इव द्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by those arrows of Drona's son, shot with the speed of the thunderbolt, enemies fell scorched like trees burned by fire."}},{"n":24,"text":"दह्यमाना महानागाः पेतुरुर्व्यां समन्ततः ।\nनदन्तो भैरवान्नादाञ्जलदोपमनिस्वनान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burning great elephants fell on the ground on every side, crying fearful cries like thunder-clouds."}},{"n":25,"text":"अपरे प्रद्रुतास्तत्र दह्यमाना महागजाः ।\nत्रेसुस्तथापरे घोरे वने दावाग्निसंवृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, great elephants on fire, ran about, and others trembled, hemmed in by wildfire as in a dreadful forest."}},{"n":26,"text":"द्रुमाणां शिखराणीव दावदग्धानि मारिष ।\nअश्ववृन्दान्यदृश्यन्त रथवृन्दानि चाभिभो ।\nअपतन्त रथौघाश्च तत्र तत्र सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Herds of horses and chariots were seen, burned like the tops of trees by a forest fire, O lord; and masses of chariots fell there in thousands."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्सैन्यं भगवानग्निर्ददाह युधि भारत ।\nयुगान्ते सर्वभूतानि संवर्तक इवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord Agni burned that army in the battle, O Bharata, like the fire of dissolution burning all beings at the end of an age."}},{"n":28,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवीं सेनां दह्यमानां महाहवे ।\nप्रहृष्टास्तावका राजन्सिंहनादान्विनेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandava army burning in the great battle, your men, O king, rejoiced and gave lion's roars."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततस्तूर्यसहस्राणि नानालिङ्गानि भारत ।\nतूर्णमाजघ्निरे हृष्टास्तावका जितकाशिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O Bharata, your men, delighted and bright, beat thousands of instruments of many kinds swiftly."}},{"n":30,"text":"कृत्स्ना ह्यक्षौहिणी राजन्सव्यसाची च पाण्डवः ।\nतमसा संवृते लोके नादृश्यत महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, the whole akshauhini and Savyasachi the Pandava were not seen in the great battle when the world was wrapped in darkness."}},{"n":31,"text":"नैव नस्तादृशं राजन्दृष्टपूर्वं न च श्रुतम् ।\nयादृशं द्रोणपुत्रेण सृष्टमस्त्रममर्षिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such a weapon, O king, as was made by furious Drona's son, we had never seen or heard of before."}},{"n":32,"text":"अर्जुनस्तु महाराज ब्राह्ममस्त्रमुदैरयत् ।\nसर्वास्त्रप्रतिघाताय विहितं पद्मयोनिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Arjuna, O great king, invoked the Brahma weapon, devised by the lotus-born for the warding off of all weapons."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तादिव तत्तमो व्युपशशाम ह ।\nप्रववौ चानिलः शीतो दिशश्च विमलाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in a moment, that darkness subsided, a cool wind blew, and the directions became clear."}},{"n":34,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम कृत्स्नामक्षौहिणीं हताम् ।\nअनभिज्ञेयरूपां च प्रदग्धामस्त्रमायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a marvel: the whole akshauhini slain and burned by the weapon's power, their forms unrecognisable."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततो वीरौ महेष्वासौ विमुक्तौ केशवार्जुनौ ।\nसहितौ संप्रदृश्येतां नभसीव तमोनुदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two heroes, great archers, Keshava and Arjuna, unharmed, were seen together like two dispellers of darkness in the sky."}},{"n":36,"text":"सपताकध्वजहयः सानुकर्षवरायुधः ।\nप्रबभौ स रथो मुक्तस्तावकानां भयंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their chariot, freed from harm with its flag, banners and horses, its fine weapons and trappings, shone, a terror to your men."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः किलकिलाशब्दः शङ्खभेरीरवैः सह ।\nपाण्डवानां प्रहृष्टानां क्षणेन समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a shout of delight arose with the sounds of conches and drums among the rejoicing Pandavas in an instant."}},{"n":38,"text":"हताविति तयोरासीत्सेनयोरुभयोर्मतिः ।\nतरसाभ्यागतौ दृष्ट्वा विमुक्तौ केशवार्जुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both armies had thought the two were slain; seeing Keshava and Arjuna come back unharmed, they were amazed."}},{"n":39,"text":"तावक्षतौ प्रमुदितौ दध्मतुर्वारिजोत्तमौ ।\nदृष्ट्वा प्रमुदितान्पार्थांस्त्वदीया व्यथिताभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two, unhurt and glad, blew their finest conches; seeing the Parthas delighted, your men were pained."}},{"n":40,"text":"विमुक्तौ च महात्मानौ दृष्ट्वा द्रौणिः सुदुःखितः ।\nमुहूर्तं चिन्तयामास किं त्वेतदिति मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the two great souls freed, Drona's son was deeply grieved, and for a moment he thought, \"What is this?\""}},{"n":41,"text":"चिन्तयित्वा तु राजेन्द्र ध्यानशोकपरायणः ।\nनिःश्वसन्दीर्घमुष्णं च विमनाश्चाभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thought, O king of kings, lost in brooding and sorrow, he sighed long and hot, and became despondent."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततो द्रौणिर्धनुर्न्यस्य रथात्प्रस्कन्द्य वेगितः ।\nधिग्धिक्सर्वमिदं मिथ्येत्युक्त्वा संप्राद्रवद्रणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son threw down his bow, leapt quickly from his chariot, said \"Shame, shame, all this is false!\" and ran away from the battle."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततः स्निग्धाम्बुदाभासं वेदव्यासमकल्मषम् ।\nआवासं च सरस्वत्याः स वै व्यासं ददर्श ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he saw Vyasa, the stainless Vedavyasa, with the sheen of a dark cloud, the dwelling of Sarasvati."}},{"n":44,"text":"तं द्रौणिरग्रतो दृष्ट्वा स्थितं कुरुकुलोद्वह ।\nसन्नकण्ठोऽब्रवीद्वाक्यमभिवाद्य सुदीनवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him standing before him, O upholder of the Kuru line, Drona's son, his voice choked, greeted him and spoke in great distress."}},{"n":45,"text":"भो भो माया यदृच्छा वा न विद्मः किमिदं भवेत् ।\nअस्त्रं त्विदं कथं मिथ्या मम कश्च व्यतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthaman said: O, is it illusion or chance? We do not know what this is. How is this weapon false, and what fault of mine is it?"}},{"n":46,"text":"अधरोत्तरमेतद्वा लोकानां वा पराभवः ।\nयदिमौ जीवतः कृष्णौ कालो हि दुरतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is this a reversal, or the defeat of the worlds, that these two Krishnas are alive? Time is hard to pass beyond."}},{"n":47,"text":"नासुरामरगन्धर्वा न पिशाचा न राक्षसाः ।\nन सर्पयक्षपतगा न मनुष्याः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither asuras, immortals, gandharvas, pishachas nor rakshasas, nor serpents, yakshas, birds or men could in any way make this weapon, sent by me, act otherwise."}},{"n":48,"text":"उत्सहन्तेऽन्यथा कर्तुमेतदस्त्रं मयेरितम् ।\nतदिदं केवलं हत्वा युक्तामक्षौहिणीं ज्वलत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This blazing weapon, after killing a whole well-armed akshauhini, was alone defeated here."}},{"n":49,"text":"केनेमौ मर्त्यधर्माणौ नावधीत्केशवार्जुनौ ।\nएतत्प्रब्रूहि भगवन्मया पृष्टो यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By what means did these two, with mortal natures, Keshava and Arjuna, not die? Lord, tell me this truly as I ask."}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":50,"text":"महान्तमेतमर्थं मां यं त्वं पृच्छसि विस्मयात् ।\nतत्प्रवक्ष्यामि ते सर्वं समाधाय मनः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"You ask me this great matter out of wonder; I shall tell it all to you, so listen with a steady mind."}},{"n":51,"text":"योऽसौ नारायणो नाम पूर्वेषामपि पूर्वजः ।\nअजायत च कार्यार्थं पुत्रो धर्मस्य विश्वकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is called Narayana, the eldest of even the ancient ones, was born for a purpose as the son of Dharma, the maker of the universe."}},{"n":52,"text":"स तपस्तीव्रमातस्थे मैनाकं गिरिमास्थितः ।\nऊर्ध्वबाहुर्महातेजा ज्वलनादित्यसंनिभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He undertook fierce austerity, standing on Mount Mainaka with raised arms, greatly radiant, like fire and the sun."}},{"n":53,"text":"षष्टिं वर्षसहस्राणि तावन्त्येव शतानि च ।\nअशोषयत्तदात्मानं वायुभक्षोऽम्बुजेक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lotus-eyed one, living on air, dried up his body for sixty thousand years and as many hundreds besides."}},{"n":54,"text":"अथापरं तपस्तप्त्वा द्विस्ततोऽन्यत्पुनर्महत् ।\nद्यावापृथिव्योर्विवरं तेजसा समपूरयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then having performed another austerity, and then again a second, greater one, he filled the space between heaven and earth with his radiance."}},{"n":55,"text":"स तेन तपसा तात ब्रह्मभूतो यदाभवत् ।\nततो विश्वेश्वरं योनिं विश्वस्य जगतः पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear son, when by that austerity he had become like Brahman, he saw the Lord of the universe, the source, the master of the whole world."}},{"n":56,"text":"ददर्श भृशदुर्दर्शं सर्वदेवैरपीश्वरम् ।\nअणीयसामणीयांसं बृहद्भ्यश्च बृहत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the Lord, very hard to see even for all the gods, smaller than the smallest and greater than the great,"}},{"n":57,"text":"रुद्रमीशानमृषभं चेकितानमजं परम् ।\nगच्छतस्तिष्ठतो वापि सर्वभूतहृदि स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rudra, the Ruler, the Bull, the Knowing, the Unborn, the Supreme, who dwells in the hearts of all beings whether moving or still,"}},{"n":58,"text":"दुर्वारणं दुर्दृशं तिग्ममन्युं\nमहात्मानं सर्वहरं प्रचेतसम् ।\nदिव्यं चापमिषुधी चाददानं\nहिरण्यवर्माणमनन्तवीर्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"hard to restrain and hard to see, of sharp wrath, the great soul, the taker of all, the wise, bearing a divine bow and two quivers, golden-armoured, of endless might,"}},{"n":59,"text":"पिनाकिनं वज्रिणं दीप्तशूलं\nपरश्वधिं गदिनं स्वायतासिम् ।\nसुभ्रुं जटामण्डलचन्द्रमौलिं\nव्याघ्राजिनं परिघं दण्डपाणिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the wielder of Pinaka, of the thunderbolt, of the blazing trident, of the axe, the mace and the long sword, fair-browed, with a moon crest in his coil of matted hair, clad in a tiger skin, holding an iron bar and a staff,"}},{"n":60,"text":"शुभाङ्गदं नागयज्ञोपवीतिं\nविश्वैर्गणैः शोभितं भूतसंघैः ।\nएकीभूतं तपसां संनिधानं\nवयोतिगैः सुष्टुतमिष्टवाग्भिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with beautiful armlets, wearing a snake as sacred thread, adorned by all the hosts and troops of beings, a gathering of austerities in one, well praised by the ageless with eloquent words,"}},{"n":61,"text":"जलं दिवं खं क्षितिं चन्द्रसूर्यौ\nतथा वाय्वग्नी प्रतिमानं जगच्च ।\nनालं द्रष्टुं यमजं भिन्नवृत्ता\nब्रह्मद्विषघ्नममृतस्य योनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"whom water, sky, heaven, earth, moon and sun, wind and fire, and the world could not behold, the unborn, of unusual conduct, destroyer of the enemies of Brahman, source of immortality,"}},{"n":62,"text":"यं पश्यन्ति ब्राह्मणाः साधुवृत्ताः\nक्षीणे पापे मनसा ये विशोकाः ।\nस तन्निष्ठस्तपसा धर्ममीड्यं\nतद्भक्त्या वै विश्वरूपं ददर्श ।\nदृष्ट्वा चैनं वाङ्मनोबुद्धिदेहैः\nसंहृष्टात्मा मुमुदे देवदेवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"whom good brahmins see, whose sins are gone and who are free of grief in mind. He, set on that, saw by austerity and devotion, the universal form, the praised dharma, and seeing the god of gods with speech, mind, intellect and body, he rejoiced with a glad soul."}},{"n":63,"text":"अक्षमालापरिक्षिप्तं ज्योतिषां परमं निधिम् ।\nततो नारायणो दृष्ट्वा ववन्दे विश्वसंभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Girt with a rosary of beads, the supreme store of lights, Narayana saw him and bowed to the source of the universe,"}},{"n":64,"text":"वरदं पृथुचार्वङ्ग्या पार्वत्या सहितं प्रभुम् ।\nअजमीशानमव्यग्रं कारणात्मानमच्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the giver of boons, the lord accompanied by Parvati of broad and lovely limbs, the unborn ruler, unflustered, the cause, the unfallen."}},{"n":65,"text":"अभिवाद्याथ रुद्राय सद्योऽन्धकनिपातिने ।\nपद्माक्षस्तं विरूपाक्षमभितुष्टाव भक्तिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having saluted Rudra, who at once strikes down Andhaka, the lotus-eyed devotee praised the three-eyed one."}},{"n":66,"text":"त्वत्संभूता भूतकृतो वरेण्य\nगोप्तारोऽद्य भुवनं पूर्वदेवाः ।\nआविश्येमां धरणीं येऽभ्यरक्ष-\nन्पुरा पुराणां तव देव सृष्टिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Narayana said: Born of you are the makers of beings, the choice ones, the guardians, the ancient gods who, entering this earth, protected your creation of old, O god."}},{"n":67,"text":"सुरासुरान्नागरक्षःपिशाचा-\nन्नरान्सुपर्णानथ गन्धर्वयक्षान् ।\nपृथग्विधान्भूतसंघांश्च विश्वां-\nस्त्वत्संभूतान्विद्म सर्वांस्तथैव ।\nऐन्द्रं याम्यं वारुणं वैत्तपाल्यं\nमैत्रं त्वाष्ट्रं कर्म सौम्यं च तुभ्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods and asuras, nagas, rakshasas and pishachas, men, garudas, gandharvas and yakshas, and the various hosts of beings, all the universe we know as born of you. The works of Indra, Yama, Varuna, Kubera, Mitra, Tvashtri and Soma are yours."}},{"n":68,"text":"रूपं ज्योतिः शब्द आकाशवायुः\nस्पर्शः स्वाद्यं सलिलं गन्ध उर्वी ।\nकामो ब्रह्मा ब्रह्म च ब्राह्मणाश्च\nत्वत्संभूतं स्थास्नु चरिष्णु चेदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Form, light, sound, ether, wind, touch, taste, water, smell, earth, desire, Brahma, the Veda and brahmins; this whole world, standing and moving, is born of you."}},{"n":69,"text":"अद्भ्यः स्तोका यान्ति यथा पृथक्त्वं\nताभिश्चैक्यं संक्षये यान्ति भूयः ।\nएवं विद्वान्प्रभवं चाप्ययं च\nहित्वा भूतानां तत्र सायुज्यमेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As drops from the waters become separate and then in dissolution merge again with them, so the knower, understanding the origin and the end of beings, leaves them and attains oneness there."}},{"n":70,"text":"दिव्यावृतौ मानसौ द्वौ सुपर्णा-\nववाक्शाखः पिप्पलः सप्त गोपाः ।\nदशाप्यन्ये ये पुरं धारयन्ति\nत्वया सृष्टास्ते हि तेभ्यः परस्त्वम् ।\nभूतं भव्यं भविता चाप्यधृष्यं\nत्वत्संभूता भुवनानीह विश्वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two divine mental birds, the pipal tree with branches below, the seven guardians, and the ten others who hold the city, are made by you, and you are beyond them. Past, future and what shall be, unassailable, all the worlds here are born of you."}},{"n":71,"text":"भक्तं च मां भजमानं भजस्व\nमा रीरिषो मामहिताहितेन ।\nआत्मानं त्वामात्मनोऽनन्यभावो\nविद्वानेवं गच्छति ब्रह्म शुक्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Favour me, your devotee who worships you; do not harm me with the harmful; one who knows thus, giving himself to you with no other thought, reaches the bright Brahman."}},{"n":72,"text":"अस्तौषं त्वां तव संमानमिच्छ-\nन्विचिन्वन्वै सवृषं देववर्य ।\nसुदुर्लभान्देहि वरान्ममेष्टा-\nनभिष्टुतः प्रतिकार्षीश्च मा माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have praised you, wishing your regard, seeking you with your bull, best of gods; grant me the very hard-to-win boons I desire, and, being praised, do not spurn me."}},{"n":73,"text":"तस्मै वरानचिन्त्यात्मा नीलकण्ठः पिनाकधृक् ।\nअर्हते देवमुख्याय प्रायच्छदृषिसंस्तुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"To him, the best of gods, deserving them, the one of inconceivable soul, the blue-throated wielder of Pinaka, praised by sages, granted the boons."}},{"text":"नीलकण्ठ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blue-throated one said:"}},{"n":74,"text":"मत्प्रसादान्मनुष्येषु देवगन्धर्वयोनिषु ।\nअप्रमेयबलात्मा त्वं नारायण भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By my favour, Narayana, among men, gods and gandharvas you will be of immeasurable strength."}},{"n":75,"text":"न च त्वा प्रसहिष्यन्ति देवासुरमहोरगाः ।\nन पिशाचा न गन्धर्वा न नरा न च राक्षसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither gods, asuras nor great serpents, nor pishachas, gandharvas, men or rakshasas will be able to withstand you,"}},{"n":76,"text":"न सुपर्णास्तथा नागा न च विश्वे वियोनिजाः ।\nन कश्चित्त्वां च देवोऽपि समरेषु विजेष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"nor garudas, nagas, or any creatures not born of a womb; no god will conquer you in battle."}},{"n":77,"text":"न शस्त्रेण न वज्रेण नाग्निना न च वायुना ।\nनार्द्रेण न च शुष्केण त्रसेन स्थावरेण वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one will harm you with weapon or thunderbolt, with fire or wind, with the wet or the dry, with the moving or the unmoving,"}},{"n":78,"text":"कश्चित्तव रुजं कर्ता मत्प्रसादात्कथंचन ।\nअपि चेत्समरं गत्वा भविष्यसि ममाधिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"in any way, by my favour, even if you go to battle and become greater than I."}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":79,"text":"एवमेते वरा लब्धाः पुरस्ताद्विद्धि शौरिणा ।\nस एष देवश्चरति मायया मोहयञ्जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know that the boons were thus obtained long ago by Shauri. This same god moves in the world deluding it with illusion."}},{"n":80,"text":"तस्यैव तपसा जातं नरं नाम महामुनिम् ।\nतुल्यमेतेन देवेन तं जानीह्यर्जुनं सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born of his austerity is the great sage called Nara; know Arjuna always as equal to this god."}},{"n":81,"text":"तावेतौ पूर्वदेवानां परमोपचितावृषी ।\nलोकयात्राविधानार्थं संजायेते युगे युगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two seers, greatly honoured among the ancient gods, are born age after age to arrange the course of the world."}},{"n":82,"text":"तथैव कर्मणः कृत्स्नं महतस्तपसोऽपि च ।\nतेजोमन्युश्च विद्वंस्त्वं जातो रौद्रो महामते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So you, wise one, great-minded, were born fierce, with the fire of wrath, from all the work and great austerity."}},{"n":83,"text":"स भवान्देववत्प्राज्ञो ज्ञात्वा भवमयं जगत् ।\nअवाकर्षस्त्वमात्मानं नियमैस्तत्प्रियेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, wise like a god, knowing the world to be made of Bhava, wore yourself down with disciplines, wishing to please him."}},{"n":84,"text":"शुभमौर्वं नवं कृत्वा महापुरुषविग्रहम् ।\nईजिवांस्त्वं जपैर्होमैरुपहारैश्च मानद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making a new, auspicious, fiery form of the Great Being, you, giver of honour, worshipped him with prayers, offerings and gifts."}},{"n":85,"text":"स तथा पूज्यमानस्ते पूर्वदेवोऽप्यतूतुषत् ।\nपुष्कलांश्च वरान्प्रादात्तव विद्वन्हृदि स्थितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Worshipped so by you, that ancient god was pleased and granted you ample boons that were in your heart, O wise one."}},{"n":86,"text":"जन्मकर्मतपोयोगास्तयोस्तव च पुष्कलाः ।\nताभ्यां लिङ्गेऽर्चितो देवस्त्वयार्चायां युगे युगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Birth, deeds, austerity and yoga are abundant in those two and in you; by them the god was worshipped in the linga, and by you in the image, age after age."}},{"n":87,"text":"सर्वरूपं भवं ज्ञात्वा लिङ्गे योऽर्चयति प्रभुम् ।\nआत्मयोगाश्च तस्मिन्वै शास्त्रयोगाश्च शाश्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who, knowing Bhava as all forms, worships the Lord in the linga, in him the yogas of the self and the eternal yogas of scripture are fulfilled."}},{"n":88,"text":"एवं देवा यजन्तो हि सिद्धाश्च परमर्षयः ।\nप्रार्थयन्ति परं लोके स्थानमेव च शाश्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus gods, siddhas and great sages worship, and ask the highest and eternal station in the world."}},{"n":89,"text":"स एष रुद्रभक्तश्च केशवो रुद्रसंभवः ।\nकृष्ण एव हि यष्टव्यो यज्ञैश्चैष सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Keshava is a devotee of Rudra and born of Rudra; Krishna, the eternal one, is the one to be worshipped with sacrifices."}},{"n":90,"text":"सर्वभूतभवं ज्ञात्वा लिङ्गेऽर्चयति यः प्रभुम् ।\nतस्मिन्नभ्यधिकां प्रीतिं करोति वृषभध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who, knowing the Lord as the source of all beings, worships him in the linga, the bull-bannered god shows greater love toward him."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":91,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा द्रोणपुत्रो महारथः ।\nनमश्चकार रुद्राय बहु मेने च केशवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, the great chariot-warrior, Drona's son, bowed to Rudra and held Keshava in high regard."}},{"n":92,"text":"हृष्टलोमा च वश्यात्मा नमस्कृत्य महर्षये ।\nवरूथिनीमभिप्रेत्य अवहारमकारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his hair standing on end and his soul subdued, he bowed to the great sage, and, looking toward his army, had the retreat sounded."}},{"n":93,"text":"ततः प्रत्यवहारोऽभूत्पाण्डवानां विशां पते ।\nकौरवाणां च दीनानां द्रोणे युधि निपातिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the withdrawal took place of the Pandavas and of the downcast Kauravas, after Drona had fallen in battle."}},{"n":94,"text":"युद्धं कृत्वा दिनान्पञ्च द्रोणो हत्वा वरूथिनीम् ।\nब्रह्मलोकं गतो राजन्ब्राह्मणो वेदपारगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having fought five days and slain the army, Drona, the brahmin who had mastered the Vedas, went to the world of Brahma, O king."}}]}]}